Hi all,

Suppose I were writing a document which is broken into chapters, each  
of which is broken into sections. It's my understanding that chapters  
would be introduced by ni'oni'oni'o, and sections with ni'oni'o.

Q1: If my document is not being spoken but written, would it be  
appropriate to use typographical elements instead of lexical elements?  
That is, could I just have large, bold, centered text indicating the  
chapter name (e.g. HTML H1), and then smaller, bold, obviously  
different text indicating the section (e.g. HTML H2)?

Q2: How do I introduce "Test #1", "Test #2", and so on? Would these be  
"le pamo'o cipra", "le remo'o cipra", etc?

Thanks!

